      ],
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/merge-base.svg",
      "description": "Bring the base branch into a pull-request branch: merge, classify every conflicted path before resolving any, refuse the whole merge if one is authored or undeclared, otherwise resolve, regenerate and prove the result with the gate set. CALLED FROM `Task_PrepareMerge` in code-change-review.bpmn, and executed by `bun run merge:main` (cat-harness/scripts/merge-base.ts). Bean `y7b3`, issue #1707. Owner, 2026-10-01: \"put in merge process bpmn\".\n\nMEASURED 2026-09-30 over 300 main-into-branch merges: 235 conflicted, 147 (63%) ONLY on generated files, each resolved the same mechanical way. The declared patterns, and why each is or is not automatic, are in the `merge-conflict-patterns` skill.\n\nALL OR NOTHING: every conflicted path is classified before any is touched, and one refusal aborts the merge and restores the tree. PROVED, NOT ASSUMED: `regen` derives every check/writer pair from the CI workflow, and an unrepaired check aborts too. Only what both gateways pass is committed.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 18,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
