      ],
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/options-analysis.svg",
      "description": "A decision reached by a NAMED methodology, with its rejected options recorded. Called as a subprocess, never run on its own.\n\nWHEN IT APPLIES: the trigger is `opening-brief`'s — IRREVERSIBILITY AND SURPRISE, not size. A reversible choice needs no subprocess; an irreversible one cannot skip it. A subprocess fired on every decision becomes ceremony, and ceremony is how a gate stops being read.\n\nWHY IT IS ONE SUBPROCESS AND NOT A BRANCH PER METHODOLOGY: the methodologies are parallel tracks selected by context, and the selection is a judgement made inside A_Select rather than a gateway. A gateway per methodology would assert the choice is computable from data, which is the claim `dmn` says to make only when the criteria recur.\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT DO: it does not decide. It produces the options, their trade-offs and a recommendation; the decision and its authorisation belong to whoever owns the calling step.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 8,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
      "name": "Options analysis",
      "nodeCount": 9,
      "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/options-analysis.bpmn",
