      ],
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/qa-publish.svg",
      "description": "How a run's derived QA results become a durable, commit-keyed record without being committed to main, and how that record is retired.\n\nYou are in this process when CI has finished the gates for a push to main or a same-repository pull request (the publish path), or when the daily retention run fires (the prune path). Both are mechanical: nothing here judges a result, and nothing here decides mergeability.\n\nThe record it writes is what a later `--against <ref>` reads as a baseline. A publish that did not happen makes that baseline UNKNOWN for every later change, which is why a red publish is still a red to fix even though it blocks nothing. Judgements are never written here: they stay on main in `test/attestations/` (owner ruling D2 (a)).",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 16,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
      "name": "Publish and keep QA results on qa-reports",
      "nodeCount": 17,
      "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/qa-publish.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/blob/main/cat-harness/processes/sdlc/qa-publish.bpmn",
