      ],
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/upstream-version-adoption.svg",
      "description": "A REUSABLE SUBPROCESS, entered once per pinned upstream dependency that has fallen behind a release. Callers invoke it with `calledElement=\"Process_UpstreamAdoption\"`; `upstream-pin-watch.bpmn` is the first, and a person may enter it directly with `workflow_start` when they want to try a version the watcher has not raised.\n\nReusable means the tenant-specific part is DATA. `upstream-pins.json` carries, per row, what of ours binds to the dependency and what its MVP runs; this diagram carries the order those are done in, which is the same for every tenant. A second tenant is a registry row, not a second diagram.\n\nShaped after `crdm-requirements.bpmn` because the question is the same one: something outside the repository wants to change what we ship, and the answer has to be a judgement somebody made on evidence rather than a merge that happened. The loop back into impact analysis is the MVP loop — findings the agent can fix are fixed on the same branch and re-evidenced, and only what remains reaches the decider.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 15,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
      "name": "Adopting an upstream version bump",
      "nodeCount": 14,
      "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/upstream-version-adoption.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/blob/main/cat-harness/processes/sdlc/upstream-version-adoption.bpmn",
